```python
import time

def stamp(func):
    t = time.time()          # runs once, at decoration time
    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):
        print("called at", t)
        return func(*args, **kwargs)
    return wrapper
```

Every call prints the same time: the moment the module was imported. The fix is to move `t = time.time()` inside `wrapper`, so it runs on each call.

